// Revised-order.
//
// Bouajjani et al., POPL 2017, Fig. 2 history (2c): a thread writes 2, then
//   reads the other thread's 1, then its own 2 again, revising the order of the
//   two writes after reading one of them.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO
//     forbids, Coherence forbids, RC11 forbids, RC17 forbids, OD-LSO forbids.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z forbids. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//     PC forbids. Coherence forbids it, and PC is stronger.
//     PRAM forbids. Slow forbids it, and PRAM is stronger.
//     Slow forbids. Local forbids it, and Slow is stronger.
//   the models' definitions:
//     CC allows. The same history is CC: each operation's causal past explains
//       its value, and a site may revise its order.
//     Causal forbids. Bouajjani et al., POPL 2017, Fig. 2 history (2c): the
//       second thread would need 2 before 1 and 1 before 2.
//     Local forbids. The thread's own view has x = 2 before both loads, so it
//       cannot return 1 and then 2 without x = 1 placed twice.
//     POCausal forbids. Whichever write is arbitrated first, a load that has
//       seen the other returns it.
//     RYW allows. The first load has seen its own x = 2 and returns x = 1, so x
//       = 2 is arbitrated before x = 1; the second load returns x = 2 and has
//       seen only it.
//     MR allows. The second load has seen x = 1 and returns x = 2, so its
//       replica orders x = 1 first; the first load constrains nothing.
//     MW allows. MW alone rejects nothing: a read sees only the write it read.
//     WFR allows. The thread writes before it reads, so writes-follow-reads
//       orders nothing.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: MRD. RA, SRA and WRA
//     are defined on release stores and acquire loads, and this program has
//     other accesses.
x := 0;
{
  x := 1
} ||| {
  x := 2;
  r0 := x;
  r1 := x
}
%%
allow (r0 = 1 && r1 = 2) [CC, RYW, MR, MW, WFR]
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 2) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO, Coherence, RC11,
                           RC11z, RC17, OD-LSO, PC, PRAM, Causal, Slow, Local,
                           POCausal]
